  "decision": "not promoted: both the shared and exact-seat action heads failed independent multidomain gates",
  "conclusion": "A replayable multi-domain dataset increased positive-regret supervision from 131 to 3379 action pairs, and offline pair accuracy reached 64-88% depending on seat. That offline fit did not transfer reliably to full games: the shared head finished 98-100 and exact-seat heads finished 100-100 against the source over their complete 500-game development-plus-confirmation evaluations. The 19x15 exact-seat confirmation regressed 9-15 paired maps while 17x13 improved 13-10, proving domain instability rather than a release-worthy universal gain.",
  "next_experiment": "Collect complete root action-value slates, including unchanged and negative alternatives, and train a conservative state-conditional ranking objective with direct-policy KL on broad replay states. The current positive-only disagreement pairs permit globally over-favoring search-like action features and are insufficient for policy improvement."
